VERDICT (no QED, Clay 0%)
  * w1(0)=s/2 : [T] at beta<1/48 (U3/P3, mod KL). Next coeff: exact normaliser part
    (-1/2 SU(3), 0 SU(2)) + amplitude part ([-c] = dressed-amplitude [R]/[O]).
  * Pade/Borel of the EXACT normaliser reach 2.5 and are positive -- but VACUOUS (M0>0).
  * w1>0 at 2.5 survives only [C] on an explicit amplitude constant C with C*u(2.5)<1;
    today C~O(10^2), C*u(2.5)>>1 at N=2,3  =>  the bracket is empty.  [O]
  * UNCONDITIONAL-shaped positivity at 2.5 holds in the large-N limit (u(2.5)->0).
